  "comment": "The boxes and the links that the command line and the editor draw for the saved views of layer `technology` and viewpoint `map` (wave 015, run 0099, issue #92; wave 016, run 0114, issue #107). One file, read by TechnologyMapTest.java (the viewpoint of the command line) and technology-map-shared.test.js (the page of a view and the page Environments, over the embedded kernel): either side drifting fails a test. A box is the id of its item (the reference of its element, or for an application deployed on a node `<node>_<application>`), a link is `from -> to` between two boxes. Both lists are sorted. A view without `plateau` is read in the only plateau of its workspace. A variant draws the same view with the `properties` it names put over those of the view: `applications` and `relationships` (both drawn when absent; false leaves out the applications deployed on the nodes, or every link) and `opened`.",
